  "summary": "Distinctive regional variations of Vietnam's iconic conical hat, each with unique materials, shapes, and decorative patterns.",
  "description": "Characterized by conical shape made from natural materials like palm leaves, sedge, or bamboo, with variations in brim size, height, and decorative elements reflecting local customs and environments. Developed across different regions of Vietnam as functional sun protection that also served as cultural identity markers and status symbols.",
  "culturalContext": "The nón lá — Vietnam's conical palm-leaf hat — carries regional identity in its geometry: Huế's \"bình định\" high cones with hidden poem-images (bài thơ) between leaf layers, Thanh Hà's 16-rim plait precision, Chuông village's satin-strap market hats, and the flat \"quai thao\" northern style against the southern \"nón bài thơ\" romance. It shades rice fields and stages áo dài elegance; craft villages sustain the palm-leaf (lá cọ) trade and UNESCO-adjacent heritage listing effort.",
